    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the greatest possible three-digit number that is divisible by both 3 and 6, we start by noting that any number divisible by 6 is automatically divisible by 3 (since 3 and 6 share common multiples). Our task thus reduces to finding the greatest two-digit number divisible by 6, as it will be the greatest three-digit number divisible by 6, and therefore divisible by both 3 and 6. \n\nTo identify this number, we begin with the greatest two-digit number and work our way down, checking the divisibility:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&99 \\div 6 = 16.5 \\quad \\text{(99 is not divisible by 6)} \\\\\n&98 \\div 6 = 16.333... \\quad \\text{(98 is not divisible by 6)} \\\\\n&97 \\div 6 = 16.166... \\quad \\text{(97 is not divisible by 6)} \\\\\n&\\vdots \\\\\n&54 \\div 6 = 9 \\quad \\text{(54 is divisible by 6)}\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nWe find that 54 is the largest two-digit number divisible by 6. Therefore, the greatest possible three-digit number that is divisible by both 3 and 6 is \\boxed{54}.",
